"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a meeting on July 15th. Key developments include the successful completion of the design phase and the first major milestone (a tested prototype for secure file sharing) ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and a budget of $2M has been approved. The project is moving into the development phase under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen, with user interface enhancements planned for October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated effective January next year. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, there are early-stage discussions regarding a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. A bug report was also received regarding a specific character issue in the system."
